3.2 Accessibility and Contrast Requirements
Target WCAG 2.2 AA contrast requirements for applicable UI elements.
For normal text:
	•	At least 4.5:1 contrast between text and background.
For large text:
	•	At least 3:1 contrast.
For meaningful non-text UI indicators, boundaries, and graphical elements:
	•	Target at least 3:1 contrast against adjacent colors where WCAG requires it.
Pay particular attention to:
	1	Line-number gutter text against the gutter background.
	2	Active line numbers against the active line background.
	3	Editor text against the editor background.
	4	Selected text against the selection background.
	5	Search matches against syntax-highlighted text.
	6	Current search matches against the editor background.
	7	Disabled and secondary controls where text remains intended to be readable.
	8	Terminal text and ANSI colors.
	9	Borders and focus indicators.
Do not assume that muted colors are accessible simply because they look visually subtle.
Measure contrast ratios mathematically and report the actual ratios for important text/background pairs in both themes.
